course: dictionary
lesson: 14420
title: Overriding: the most important thing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Overriding can be an adjective that describes the one thing that matters more than anything else. «Safety is the overriding concern on the school trip.» Nothing else counts as much as safety. Words like concern, aim, priority and importance nearby are clues.
explain: Overriding can also be the -ing form of the verb override. To override something is to cancel it or take control of it. «The teacher was overriding the old rule to let us play outside.» The teacher stopped the old rule from applying that day.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «Her overriding priority was finishing on time» means her most important job was finishing on time, and that makes sense. If the meaning does not fit, look again at whether the word describes a thing or shows an action.
fact: Overriding (adjective) means more important than anything else.
fact: Common phrases: overriding concern, overriding importance, overriding priority.
fact: Override (verb) means to cancel or take control of a decision, setting or machine.
fact: «Our overriding aim» means the most important aim.
fact: «She was overriding the setting on the oven» means she was taking control of the setting.
exercise: «Safety is the overriding concern on the school trip.» What does overriding mean here? | Lost | Cancelled | Very loud | *More important than anything else
exercise: «The teacher was overriding the old rule to let us play outside.» What does overriding mean here? | Making the rule longer | Forgetting the rule about lunch | *Cancelling or taking control of a decision | Copying the rule into a book
exercise: «Her overriding priority was finishing her project on time.» Which phrase means the same as overriding priority? | Favourite colour | *Most important job | Smallest worry | Last thing on the list
test: «The overriding importance of kindness shows in everything we do.» What does overriding mean? | Less important than the rest | Written in red | *More important than anything else | Hidden
test: «He was overriding the setting on the washing machine.» What does overriding mean here? | Forgetting the setting | Admiring the setting | *Taking manual control of the setting | Copying the setting into a book
exam: Which sentence uses overriding as an adjective meaning most important? | «The rule was overridden by the teacher.» | «The machine was overriding its settings.» | *«Our overriding aim is to be kind.» | «She was overriding the rule.»
